        "body.py: added posterior_wall(v, B, xc) -> (slope, info), which reads the wall on the lattice. Its pieces are short functions: kept_wall, read_wall, wall_window, scan_step_back, wall_edges, backmost_bone, most_posterior_per_line, wall_design, trimmed_start, biweight, wall_freedom, wall_slope_range, clean_digitisation, wall_flags and degrees_of. Every constant is a commented WALL_* constant. The docstring covers the staircase, the cut, the window, the gate, the fit, the clamp, the freedom and its bound, and the refusals, with the numbers I measured on the 98 cached phantom vertebrae.",
        "body.py: posterior_wall_slope now returns posterior_wall(...)[0], so it is NAN on a refusal instead of 0.0.",
        "body.py: the reading is cached on the vertebra as v._posterior_wall, keyed on frame identity, v.loc identity, xc equality and np.array_equal(B). A different B, xc, frame or label reads it again.",
        "body.py: measures adds wall_flags. 'posterior_wall' gives the reason when the wall is refused, and both inclinations go NAN, because a NaN slope passes through atan. 'posterior_wall_free' is set when the freedom passes WALL_FREE_FLAG_DEG (3 degrees).",
        "body.py: the module docstring now says how the inclinations' wall is read. No import cycle: body imports only anatomy and scanimport, and the pedicle bound is held here as WALL_FREEDOM_DEG = 9.0.",
