        "file": "morphometry/body.py",
        "line": 411,
        "detail": "I made the suite's notch phantom a little bigger: P.lumbar(notch_w=8, notch_h=6, notch_d=5), against the suite's 5 x 6 x 4, on the suite's grid (column tilted 18 degrees, grid turned 7). On 1 mm slices posterior_wall reads 29.15 degrees off. It keeps 62 edges and drops 118, and gives a freedom of 0.51. On 2.5 mm slices it reads +29.49 off, keeping 25 and dropping 55, freedom 2.10. Both stay under WALL_FREE_FLAG_DEG, so measures sets no posterior_wall flag and nothing is refused. The angles downstream take the error with them. On 1 mm slices: endplate_incl +29.05, endplate_lower_incl +29.61, left pedicle_angle_sagittal +29.07, all against a truth of 0, and spinous_angle -8.32 against +20. On 2.5 mm slices: endplate_incl -29.29 and spinous_angle +48.51. None of these carries a flag. Other silent errors: 8x8x4 on thick slices -4.45 (freedom 2.85); 8x8x5 on thick slices -2.98 (freedom 2.89); 8x8x5 on thick slices with the grid near the frame (x2) -29.73. That last one is flagged only as free, since its freedom is 7.24. The cause: the trimmed fit keeps 75 per cent, so once the notch floor holds more than a quarter of the edges, the fit can be a line that joins the floor to part of the wall. The span check passes (9.6 to 11 mm of a 16 mm window). The label does not part, so the freedom comes from a clean digitisation of that wrong fit (clean_digitisation), and that says nothing about whether the fit is the wall. The reader at a9f21fd was also off on these notches (-22.48 and -15.12), so this is not a regression. But the new reader's refusals and freedom report confidence they do not have. One tell does separate these cases: the share of the band's edges more than a step off the fit. It is 0.43 to 0.69 on every notch reading off by 2.98 to 29.7 degrees. It is 0.00 on all 98 clean cached vertebrae, and at most 0.36 on the 1,172 readings within 1.5 degrees in the implementer's robustness runs (impl/robust_0.json, robust_1.json). Scripts and logs: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f/scratchpad/wall/review_geometry/notches.py, notch_downstream.py (nd_thin.log, nd_thick.log), tells.py (tells_n1.log to tells_n3.log, tells_cache.log), old_on_notch.py.",
        "fix": "In read_wall, refuse with a reason where more than about 40 per cent of the band's edges lie more than a step off the fitted surface (the dropped share computed as (~good).mean()). On the measured sets this refuses every silent notch failure and no reading within 1.5 degrees, except the 5x10x4 thin notch (share 0.51, which reads -0.19). Then add the 8x6x5 notch to BasivertebralNotch as a refusal test.",
        "lens": "geometry",
        "votes": [
          {
            "refuted": false,
            "reason": "The claim holds. I rebuilt the phantoms with the suite's own helpers instead of the reviewer's: test_morphometry.built and wall_error, strict drawing, and measure_volume's rows for the downstream values. Every number the reviewer gave came back. The trimmed fit lets the notch floor pull it onto a line about 29 degrees off. The wall is not refused. The freedom passes both bounds. On the two suite-grid cases the rows carry no posterior_wall flag and no spinous flag.\n\nThe failure comes from the change's own reader, read_wall, not from the phantom or a harness detail. The code half-admits the limit: the comment on WALL_TRIM_KEEP says a notch holding more of the edges \"is not told from the wall\". But nothing in the output says so. The freedom from clean_digitisation of the fitted surface looks tight, because it describes how well the lattice pins that wrong surface, not whether the surface is the wall.\n\nThe reviewer's cause also holds. On 8x6x5, thin, the notch floor holds 67 of the 180 edges (share 0.37). The trimmed cost of the start the reader found (slope -23.99 degrees, cost 205.3) is lower than the cost of the wall's own edges fitted alone (-0.41 degrees, cost 277.2). So with 75 per cent kept, least trimmed squares prefers the wrong line. The biweight then takes it to -29.15.\n\nIt is not a regression: the reader at a9f21fd was also off, by -22.48 (thin) and -15.13 (thick). The title's \"about 29 degrees\" is the worst case, not the rule: other oversized notches read 3 to 4.5 degrees off. A 5x10x4 notch with share 0.51 reads only -0.19, which the reviewer reports himself. Nothing was run on a real mask.",
            "measured": "All runs are on phantoms. Scripts and logs are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f/scratchpad/wall/verify_0_0/: notch_check.py, cause.py and old.py.\n\n**8x6x5 notch, suite grid (column tilted 18, grid turned 7)**\n- 1 mm slices: the wall reads -29.15 degrees off. It keeps 62 edges and drops 118 (share 0.66). Freedom 0.51, parted False, nothing refused.\n  - In measure_volume's rows: endplate_incl +29.05, endplate_lower_incl +29.61, left pedicle_angle_sagittal +29.07 (all against a truth of 0), spinous_angle -8.32 against +20.\n  - The only flag is pedicle_right (\"surfaces stand under 2 columns\"). There is no posterior_wall, posterior_wall_free or spinous flag.\n- 2.5 mm slices: the wall reads +29.49 off. It keeps 25 and drops 55 (share 0.69). Freedom 2.10.\n  - In the rows: endplate_incl -29.29, endplate_lower_incl -29.18, spinous_angle +48.51.\n  - The only flags are on the pedicles' climbs. There is no wall or spinous flag.\n\n**Cause, 1 mm slices** (from cause.py)\n- The notch floor holds 67 of the 180 edges (share 0.37).\n- The canal line leans -23.56 degrees. The gate's reach is 4.82 mm and the window is 16.2 mm.\n- The trimmed start reads -23.99 degrees at a trimmed cost of 205.3. The biweight takes it to -29.15 (cost 284.4).\n- The wall's own edges fitted alone read -0.41 degrees at a trimmed cost of 277.2.\n- Of the 62 edges within a step of the final fit, 35 are wall and 27 notch.\n\n**Cause, 2.5 mm slices**\n- The notch floor holds 29 of the 80 edges (share 0.36).\n- The start reads +27.54 at cost 111.0. The wall's own fit reads +1.01 at cost 134.1.\n\n**The reviewer's other cases** (thick slices)\n- 8x8x4, suite grid: -4.45 off, freedom 2.85, share 0.52.\n- 8x8x5, suite grid: -2.98 off, freedom 2.89, share 0.43.\n- 8x8x5, near-aligned grid (tilted 2 about x): -29.73 off, freedom 7.24.\n  - It carries only the flag posterior_wall_free. That flag says the angles may be off \"by up to half\" of 7.2 degrees, yet endplate_incl and endplate_lower_incl read +31.73 and spinous_angle -9.34 against +20.\n\n**Control: the suite's own 5x6x4 notch**\n- 1 mm: -0.20 off, share 0.20, freedom 0.35.\n- 2.5 mm: +0.36 off, share 0.22, freedom 0.60.\n\n**Reader at a9f21fd on 8x6x5:** -22.48 (thin), -15.13 (thick).\n\n**Clean cache:** the reviewer's log tells_cache.log covers all 98 cached vertebrae, and the largest dropped share there is 0.00."
          },
          {
            "refuted": false,
            "reason": "The claim holds. I re-measured it with the suite's own helpers (test_morphometry.built, which draws with strict=True, and wall_error) and the phantom's own truth, not the reviewer's storage_order helpers. The numbers match the reviewer's to the hundredth.\n\nThe cause is the one the reviewer names. In the phantom's own frame, the 8x6x5 notch's floor holds 31 per cent of the band's edges on thin slices (55 of 180) and 33 per cent on thick (26 of 80). The wall holds only 63 to 64 per cent, which is less than the 75 per cent the trimmed fit keeps. So the trimmed fit plus the biweight settles on a surface that joins part of the floor to one end of the wall:\n- thin: it keeps 25 floor edges at phantom z -2.9 to 0.0 and 35 wall edges at z 5.1 to 8.1;\n- thick: it keeps 9 floor edges at z 1.8 to 2.7 and 15 wall edges at z -7.0 to -4.6.\n\nThe same fit on the wall's edges alone reads -0.43 and +1.07 degrees. On the suite's 5x6x4 notch the floor holds only 18 to 21 per cent of the edges, the fit keeps none of them, and it reads within 0.25 degrees.\n\nNothing in the reader catches this:\n- The label does not part (parted False), so the freedom comes from clean_digitisation of the wrong fit, and it is small: 0.51 thin, 2.10 thick.\n- The span check passes: 11.0 and 9.6 mm of a 16.2 mm window, against a need of 8.1.\n- No flag is set, and spinous_angle carries no flag.\n\nThe limit is only half documented. posterior_wall's docstring promises robustness only below \"a quarter of the edges\", and WALL_TRIM_KEEP's comment says a notch holding more \"is not told from the wall\". But neither says the error can reach about 29 degrees with no flag, and the list of known failures names only the lip and ragged edges.\n\nThe reviewer's proposed tell checks out on the implementer's robustness rows (impl/robust_0.json and robust_1.json). Of the 1,271 readings, 1,172 are within 1.5 degrees, and their largest dropped share is 0.358. None of them is over 0.4.\n\nThe defect does arise from code that runs. My scripts and logs are in /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f/scratchpad/wall/verify_0_1/ (notch_check.py, mechanism.py, thin_suite.log, thick_suite.log, thick_x2.log, mech_thin.log, mech_thick.log).",
            "measured": "Measured on phantoms only, P.lumbar notch phantom, L3, built by test_morphometry.built.\n\nSuite grid (tilt 18 degrees, turn 7), thin slices (0.8 x 0.8 x 1 mm), notch 8,6,5:\n- wall error -29.15, 62 edges kept, 118 dropped (share 0.66), span 11.0 mm, freedom 0.51, parted False, no why;\n- endplate_incl +29.05, endplate_lower_incl +29.61 and pedicle_angle_sagittal_left +29.07, each against a truth of 0;\n- spinous_angle -8.32 against +20;\n- body flags {} and spinous flag None.\n\nSuite grid, thin slices, notch 5,6,4 (the suite's own):\n- wall error -0.20, share 0.20, freedom 0.35, parted True;\n- endplate_incl +0.08.\n\nSuite grid, thick slices (0.86 x 0.86 x 2.5 mm):\n- notch 8,6,5: wall error +29.49, 25 kept, 55 dropped (share 0.69), span 9.6, freedom 2.10, parted False; endplate_incl -29.29, endplate_lower_incl -29.18, spinous_angle +48.51; no flags.\n- notch 8,8,4: wall error -4.45, share 0.52, freedom 2.85; endplate_incl +5.91; no flags.\n- notch 5,6,4: wall error +0.36, share 0.22.\n\nGrid x2 (tilt 2 degrees about x), thick slices, notch 8,8,5:\n- wall error -29.73, share 0.50, freedom 7.24;\n- the only flag is posterior_wall_free;\n- endplate_incl +31.73.\n\nWhere the edges lie, in the phantom's frame:\n- thin 8,6,5: 55 of 180 on the notch floor (0.31) and 113 on the wall (0.63). The fit keeps 25 floor edges (z -2.9 to 0.0) and 35 wall edges (z 5.1 to 8.1). On the wall's edges alone it reads -0.43.\n- thick 8,6,5: 26 of 80 on the floor (0.33) and 51 on the wall (0.64). The fit keeps 9 floor and 15 wall edges. On the wall alone it reads +1.07.\n- 5,6,4: the floor holds 0.18 (thin) and 0.21 (thick) of the edges, and the fit keeps none of them.\n\nWindow and gate: the window is 16.2 mm, the half band 5.73, the reach 4.82 thin and 4.49 thick, and the canal line leans -23.56 (thin) and -14.01 (thick) degrees.\n\nThe dropped-share tell over the 1,271 readings in impl/robust_0.json and robust_1.json: 1,172 are within 1.5 degrees, with a largest share of 0.358, and none over 0.4.\n\nThe cited line, body.py 411, is `good = np.abs(r) <= step_y` in read_wall."
