ite checks only the 0.5-degree bound on two phantoms.\n\nOne part is slightly overstated. \"No file names the configurations\" is too strong: the docstring names them loosely, and the two spacings appear in the suite. They are not tied to the cache there, though, and this does not change the finding.\n\nMeasured as a side check: does the committed phantom draw what the scratch cache drew? Yes. phantom.py's new lean parameter matches build_cache.sheared voxel for voxel. On the x2 and suite18 grids, at lean +5 and -5, on both thin and thick spacing, 0 voxels differed and the affines were equal. So the phantom comment (\"as the wall-slope study of 30 October drew it\") is true, and committing a record of the configuration list (or the scorer) would be enough to rebuild the cache. That supports the reviewer's fix; it does not refute the defect.",
            "measured": "The committed P.lumbar(lean=L) against build_cache.sheared(L), on grids x2 and suite18, L = +5 and -5, thin (0.8x0.8x1) and thick (0.86x0.86x2.5): 8 drawings, 0 voxels differing in each (23945415 / 8464918 voxels on x2, 32804200 / 11466126 on suite18), affines equal. Script: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f/scratchpad/wall/verify_9_0/same_drawing.py; log: /tmp/claude-0/-home-user/cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f/scratchpad/wall/verify_9_0/same_drawing.log. The grep results above were run over /home/user/bordercall, excluding archive/ and .git."
