      {
        "title": "No test pins the clamp: the whole suite passes with it taken out",
        "severity": "medium",
        "file": "morphometry/tests/test_morphometry.py",
        "line": 24,
        "detail": "I patched wall_freedom to report every label as unparted, so b is just the fitted slope (/tmp/claude-0/-home-user/cbdcd57f-bcf8-5a71-ab64-4f0b9fbdb74f/scratchpad/wall/review_tests/mutants.py noclamp, log mut_noclamp.log). All 31 tests still pass. On LeanedWall's L3 the fit reads 4.528 degrees against the frame-corrected truth of 4.934, an error of -0.406. The clamp lifts it to the low end of the parted range, 4.837 (error -0.097). WALL_TOL_DEG = 0.5 accepts both readings. Over the suite's 29 wall readings the clamp moves the slope in 12 of them, by at most 0.571 degrees (a 2.5 mm L4 that no test asserts on). It moves the notch's reading by 0.04 and ThickSlices' L3 not at all. So the clamp can break without any test failing.\n\nChecked and sound, no separate finding:\n(1) Against the base reader (a9f21fd taken by git archive into review_tests/base, the new phantom and tests copied in, removed afterwards), every new test fails once the names it calls are mapped onto the old reading. LeanedWall reads -3.05 against 0.5. The notch wall reads -18.17 and its endplate_incl 18.05. ThickSlices endplate_incl reads 4.55 (its wall 4.51 off). The refusal test fails with KeyError 'posterior_wall'. Without that mapping, three tests error on missing names and two fail on their numbers (4.55 and 18.05).\n(2) On this tree the readings are: LeanedWall 0.10, notch wall 0.21, notch inclinations 0.08 and 0.17, ThickSlices inclinations 0.15 and 0.01 with its wall 0.19.\n(3) The phantom change moves no old truth. The straight, shapes and thick phantoms draw the same labels voxel for voxel under both phantom.py versions, and truth() gives the same values.\n(4) The suite is green: 31 tests in 444.3 s (real 7m25s), alone apart from two probes of about a minute each. The base's 26 tests took 399.1 s alongside three other processes.\n(5) There is one wall reading per measured vertebra (29 readings for 29 vertebrae).",
        "fix": "Bound LeanedWall's wall error at 0.25 degrees, with a comment giving the measured 0.10 clamped and 0.41 unclamped. Or assert on the reading's record directly: info['parted'] is true, fitted_deg lies below free_lo_deg, and the slope equals free_lo_deg.",
        "lens": "tests",
        "votes": [
          {
            "refuted": false,
            "reason": "The claim holds: no test fails when the clamp is taken out. I wrote my own mutant, separate from the reviewer's (verify_10_0/noclamp_run.py). It rebuilds body.read_wall from its own source with line 418, `b = min(max(float(coef[1]), b_lo), b_hi) if parted else float(coef[1])`, replaced by `b = float(coef[1])`. Unlike the reviewer's patch of wall_freedom, it leaves the record's parted, free_lo/hi and free_deg as the tree writes them, so the freedom refusal and the flag work as before. I ran morphometry.tests.test_morphometry together with every other test module that imports morphometry (morphoview.tests.test_lines, maskedge.tests.test_disc, maskedge.tests.test_edge). All 54 tests passed with no failures or errors, and the run made 30 wall readings. On the three fixtures the new tests assert on (verify_10_0/fixtures_probe.py), LeanedWall's L3 wall error is -0.097 clamped and -0.406 unclamped. The fitted 4.528 is clamped up to 4.837 against a truth of 4.934, inside a parted range of [4.837, 5.131], and WALL_TOL_DEG = 0.5 accepts both. On the notch the error is -0.205 clamped and -0.245 unclamped. On ThickSlices' L3 the clamp moves nothing: +0.188 either way, with a range of [-0.555, 1.030]. The morphoview and maskedge tests check that lines agree with values, and only the wedge is drawn as an angle, so none of them reaches the clamp. The reviewer's figures reproduce: all 30 readings parted, and the clamp moves 13 of them (12 in the morphometry suite plus one in the morphoview test). The largest move is 0.571 degrees, on an L4 (fitted -1.189, clamped -0.618), followed by 0.327 and 0.309 (LeanedWall's L3). So the clamp can break and the suite stays green. The fix the reviewer suggests would catch it: bound LeanedWall at 0.25 against the measured 0.097 clamped and 0.406 unclamped, or assert on info['parted'] and the slope equal to free_lo_deg.",
            "measured": "Clamp taken out of read_wall (line 418 only): 54 tests (31 morphometry, 10 morphoview, 13 maskedge) ran in 541 s with no failures or errors; log in verify_10_0/noclamp_all.log, readings in verify_10_0/noclamp_all.json. LeanedWall L3 wall error: -0.097 clamped, -0.406 unclamped (truth 4.934, fitted 4.528, range [4.837, 5.131], bound 0.5). Notch L3: -0.205 clamped, -0.245 unclamped. ThickSlices L3: +0.188 both ways. Of 30 readings, all parted and the clamp moves 13, by at most 0.571 (L4), then 0.327 and 0.309; log in verify_10_0/clamp_moves.log."
          }
        ]
